results.model_answer:
Within nine months of the September 2023 System‑Based Audit (SBA) guideline (see Document 9), the June 2024 SRO 2024‑67 (Documents 1, 2, 3 & 4) required every AEO to:

* maintain a full, customs‑relevant audit trail of all accounting and movement data and describe its essential features (Doc 1 §5 & Doc 2 §3.1.1);  
* specify the hardware/software used for customs business and demonstrate segregation of functions (development, testing, operation), user‑role separation, strict access‑control lists and traceability between the internal business system and the customs declaration system (Doc 1 §3.2.1 / Doc 2 §3.2.1);  
* be able to distinguish between duty‑paid and duty‑suspended goods and record their exact locations (Doc 1 §3.2.2); and  
* have documented procedures for notifying customs or other OGAs of any irregularities (suspicion of theft, smuggling, etc.) and record any such notifications (Doc 3 §3.5.2).  

These operational controls were added to ensure the SBA could be applied effectively to AEOs.

