Less than a month after the 21 January 2025 physical‑examination guidance, the AEO Guidelines were expanded with a series of security‑focused items, namely:

* a requirement to state whether a security‑service provider is used and, if so, to provide its threat‑assessment report (clause 5.1.8);  
* a requirement to describe any security or safety conditions imposed by customers or insurers (clause 5.1.9);  
* detailed description of how the external boundary of the premises is secured, how fence‑ and building‑checks are carried out, recorded and verified, and how security incidents are reported and dealt with (clause 5.2.1);  
* a procedure for handling unauthorized persons or vehicles on the site, how it is communicated to staff and documented (clause 5.3.2), together with a site plan and information on co‑located entities (clauses 5.3.3‑5.3.4); and  
* a description of how goods in the warehousing area are protected against unauthorized access, how compliance is checked and whether a written procedure exists (clause 5.7.4).

